        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Micky Dolenz, George Michael Dolenz Jr., Jesse James Dupree, Samantha Juste, Jacki Bond\n- Organizations: the Monkees, Jackyl, BBC, Top of the Pops, Strike, Go\n- Roles: actor, musician, television director, radio personality, theater director, vocalist, drummer, lead singer, guitarist, songwriter, co-host, vocalist\n\nFacts:\n- George Michael Dolenz Jr., known as Micky Dolenz, was born on March 8, 1945.\n- Micky Dolenz is an American actor, musician, television director, radio personality, and theater director.\n- Micky Dolenz was best known as a vocalist and drummer of the 1960s pop/rock band the Monkees.\n- In 1968, Samantha Juste married Micky Dolenz of the Monkees.\n- In 1991, Jesse James Dupree founded the rock band Jackyl.\n- Jesse James Dupree is the lead singer, guitarist, and primary songwriter in Jackyl.\n- Samantha Juste co-hosted BBC television's Top of the Pops.\n- Jacki Bond came from South London.\n- Jacki Bond and Samantha Juste were the two British female vocalists signed to Strike or, in Juste's case, its subsidiary Go.",
